- `.csarc/config.yml` holds the saved CSARC settings; change them only with `csarc update --data KEY=VALUE`.
{% if documentation_mode == 'off' -%}
- Use the linked Issue for scope; `.csarc/docs/csarc.md` is the stable operations entry point because project documentation is disabled.
{% else -%}
- Use the linked Issue or `docs/specs/` SDD contract for scope; `docs/README.md` maps durable project memory. Use `docs/adr/` for decisions; also search a project-owned `docs/decisions/` and never move it.
- Follow [`.csarc/docs/documentation-policy.md`](documentation-policy.md). Before a non-Draft pull request is delivered, compare changed behavior and configuration with project documentation and record `aligned` or a reasoned `not-applicable` against the exact head; `drift` and `inconclusive` block delivery.
- In an adopt or update pull request, copy every `Policy documentation` report row into the documentation-review reason, keep `drift` or `inconclusive` until each blocking row is resolved, and never rewrite project-owned text without owner approval.
{% endif -%}
- Root `SECURITY.md` is scanner policy; `.github/SECURITY.md` is the human vulnerability-disclosure policy. [`.csarc/docs/security-scanner-readiness.md`](security-scanner-readiness.md) lists AI security scanner commands and limits.
